<Page
  title="Cookie Policy"
  heading="Cookie Policy"
  description="How bla5k uses cookies and similar technologies, and how you can manage your consent — GDPR-compliant."
  updated="August 2026"
>
  <p>
    This Cookie Policy explains how <strong>bla5k</strong> uses cookies and similar
    technologies, why we use them, and how you can control or withdraw your consent — in
    line with the <strong>GDPR</strong> (EU Regulation 2016/679) and the
    <strong>ePrivacy Directive</strong>.
  </p>

  <h2>What are cookies?</h2>
  <p>
    Cookies are small text files stored on your device when you visit a website. They help
    the site work, remember your preferences, and — where you consent — understand how the
    site is used. Some storage happens through similar technologies such as localStorage.
  </p>

  <h2>Consent</h2>
  <p>
    When you first visit bla5k, a consent banner asks you to choose how we may use cookies.
    You can <strong>Accept all</strong>, <strong>Reject non-essential</strong>, or adjust
    your choice at any time by clearing the site's storage in your browser. Your choice is
    remembered for future visits, and you can change it at any time.
  </p>

  <h2>Cookies we use</h2>

  <h3>1. Strictly necessary</h3>
  <p>
    These are required for the Site to function and cannot be switched off. bla5k is a
    static directory and has very few of these — mainly preferences stored locally so we
    remember your consent choice and your directory search state.
  </p>

  <h3>2. Analytics (optional)</h3>
  <p>
    We use two analytics tools, both <strong>loaded only after you accept</strong>:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Cloudflare Web Analytics</strong> — a privacy-first, <strong>cookieless</strong>
      service that aggregates page views, referrers, and approximate country-level traffic
      without identifiers. If you reject analytics, the beacon is disabled for you.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Google Analytics 4 (GA4)</strong> — used to understand how the Site is found
      and used. GA4 uses cookies and may collect device and usage data processed by Google.
      It is <strong>never loaded unless you accept</strong>, and you can withdraw consent at
      any time.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h3>3. Advertising (optional)</h3>
  <p>
    We may display advertising through <strong>Google AdSense</strong>. If and when ads are
    enabled, Google may use cookies to serve ads based on your prior visits, including
    personalized ads. These cookies are <strong>only loaded after you give consent</strong>.
    You can opt out of personalized advertising at
    <a href="https://www.google.com/settings/ads" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Ads Settings</a>
    and learn more at
    <a href="https://www.aboutads.info" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">aboutads.info</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>How to manage or delete cookies</h2>
  <p>You can control cookies through your browser settings:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Chrome:</strong> Settings → Privacy and security → Cookies.</li>
    <li><strong>Firefox:</strong> Settings → Privacy &amp; Security → Cookies and Site Data.</li>
    <li><strong>Safari:</strong> Preferences → Privacy → Manage Website Data.</li>
    <li><strong>Edge:</strong> Settings → Cookies and site permissions.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    You can also use your browser's private/incognito mode, or install an ad-blocker or
    privacy extension to limit cookies across sites.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights under GDPR</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>The right to <strong>withdraw consent</strong> at any time.</li>
    <li>The right to <strong>access</strong> the data we hold about you.</li>
    <li>The right to <strong>rectification</strong>, <strong>erasure</strong> ("right to be forgotten"), and <strong>portability</strong>.</li>
    <li>The right to <strong>object</strong> to processing, and to <strong>restrict</strong> it.</li>
    <li>The right to <strong>lodge a complaint</strong> with your local data-protection authority.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    To exercise any of these rights, contact us via the <a href="/contact/">Contact</a>
    page. We respond to valid requests promptly, usually within 30 days.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this Cookie Policy from time to time. The "last updated" date at the top
    reflects the most recent revision. Continued use of the Site after a change means you
    accept the updated policy.
  </p>

